// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! D-DX5-HOOK1=A (Tower #549) — compiler-extension v1 host surface.
//RS //!
//RS //! Reuses the shipped WASM Component Model substrate (`WASMTIME_CRATE_SPEC` +
//RS //! `Prelude/CompilerExtension.rs`) in the isolated sibling `jetpack` process,
//RS //! with a **compiler-specific** WIT world
//RS //! that stays distinct from:
//RS //! - application `target: sandbox` / `core.plugin` (world `jetplugin`, D-PLUGIN1)
//RS //! - PATH-discovered `jet-*` helpers (D-DX5)
//RS //!
//RS //! V1 contract (ratified): post-sema typed read-only snapshot in → validated
//RS //! findings/edit proposals out. The host remains the only semantic authority;
//RS //! plugins cannot mutate compiler state or expose rustc (I2/I3).
//RS //!
//RS //! # Protocol (exact)
//RS //!
//RS //! Wire bytes for `analyze(snapshot) -> response` are UTF-8 DataTree values with
//RS //! **deterministic key order** (lexicographic) and no insignificant whitespace.
//RS //! Schema version is `protocol` (must equal [`PROTOCOL_VERSION`]).
//RS //!
//RS //! Snapshot fields: `protocol`, `stage`, `abilities`, `limits`, `trust`,
//RS //! `types`, `symbols`, `spans`, `host_imports` (symbols carry `effects` +
//RS //! `provenance`; type facts carry structural shape metadata).
//RS //!
//RS //! # Limits / trust / lifecycle
//RS //!
//RS //! - [`ResourceLimits`]: fuel, memory, table, finding/edit/response caps, wall timeout.
//RS //! - [`TrustPolicy`]: components are `untrusted` by default; protocol + ability
//RS //!   negotiation must pass before analyze.
//RS //! - **Deterministic sandbox:** empty host linker — no clock/random/fs/net/process
//RS //!   imports; guests that declare them fail closed at load (D-DX5-HOOK1).
//RS //! - [`ExtensionSession`]: Idle → Loaded → (optional staged response) → Closed.
//RS //!   Staging never mutates compiler facts; [`ExtensionSession::rollback`] discards
//RS //!   staged output only (accept latch stays final); [`ExtensionSession::close`]
//RS //!   invokes a guest closer (host passes `jet_compiler_extension_close`) so
//RS //!   guest Store/memory is dropped.
//RS 
//RS use crate::FFI::WASMTIME_CRATE_SPEC;
//RS use jet_foundation::Authority::HostImportFact;
//RS use jet_foundation::DataTree::DataTree;
//RS use crate::JSON;
//RS use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};
//RS 
